#original-page(595.276pt, 841.89pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(519.292pt, 793.74pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 116.705pt, "1. Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 144.596pt, "Freestanding thin films refer to ultrathin materials (ranging from nanoscale to microscale thickness) ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 164.703pt, "that maintain structural and functional integrity without the need for a supporting substrate [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(503.876pt, 164.703pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(509.699pt, 164.703pt, ",")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(512.57pt, 164.703pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(518.393pt, 164.703pt, "]. ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 184.857pt, "The initial realization and formal introduction of freestanding films can be traced back to 1966 and ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 204.965pt, "1978, with chemical exfoliation emerging as the earliest method for fabricating flexible films [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(506.758pt, 204.965pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(512.57pt, 204.965pt, ",")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(515.511pt, 204.965pt, "4")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(521.276pt, 204.965pt, "]. ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 225.119pt, "In early studies, the concept of “freestanding” primarily denoted the geometric independence of ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 245.215pt, "the material from a substrate, characterized by a broad thickness range (micrometers to ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 265.38pt, "millimeters), where mechanical stability was maintained by macroscopic structural design. This ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 285.476pt, "definition was widely adopted in subsequent research following the 1990 GaAs nanowire studies ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 305.642pt, "[")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(73.918pt, 305.642pt, "5-8")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(89.521pt, 305.642pt, "]: examples include InP membranes formed via bonding-and-release processes [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(458.514pt, 305.642pt, "9")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(464.279pt, 305.642pt, "], and thicker ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 325.738pt, "films such as nanosheets/fibers or polymer membranes produced by spin-coating [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(479.87pt, 325.738pt, "10")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(491.517pt, 325.738pt, ",")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(494.458pt, 325.738pt, "11")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(506.093pt, 325.738pt, "] or ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 345.903pt, "electrospinning [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(154.803pt, 345.903pt, "12-14")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(181.982pt, 345.903pt, "]. These fabrication strategies were primarily aimed at achieving ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 365.999pt, "transferability, but they overlooked two critical aspects: the evolution of interfacial stresses during ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 386.165pt, "heterogeneous integration, and the inherent bulk-like properties exhibited by the materials due to ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 406.261pt, "their thickness limitations, rendering them fundamentally distinct from truly ultrathin systems.")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 434.164pt, "With the rapid advancement of nanotechnology and advanced devices, research on freestanding ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 454.318pt, "thin films has garnered unprecedented attention, emerging as a pivotal frontier for overcoming ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 474.425pt, "performance limitations in conventional materials and devices. Traditional thin films, constrained ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 494.579pt, "by substrate lattice matching, thermal expansion coefficient mismatch, and interfacial effects ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 514.675pt, "(termed the “substrate clamping effect”), often exhibit suppressed or distorted intrinsic ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 534.841pt, "physicochemical properties (e.g., ferroelectricity, ferromagnetism, superconductivity, mechanical ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 554.936pt, "flexibility, optical response) [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(208.134pt, 554.936pt, "15-24")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(235.314pt, 554.936pt, "]. ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 582.839pt, "The core value of freestanding films lies in their “substrate-free” nature—fully liberating the ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 603.005pt, "intrinsic properties of materials at low-dimensional limits while providing revolutionary design ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 623.101pt, "freedom for material engineering and device architecture. These films can be precisely transferred, ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 643.255pt, "stacked, folded, or curled as independent units, enabling van der Waals (vdW) heterostructures ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 663.362pt, "[")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(73.918pt, 663.362pt, "25")
