  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(519.292pt, 793.74pt, "5")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 116.705pt, "developed diverse physical delamination methodologies to obtain freestanding thin films. This ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 136.8pt, "section details representative techniques including laser lift-off, mechanical exfoliation, and ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 156.966pt, "remote epitaxy vdW lift-off. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 184.857pt, "2.1.1 Laser Lift-Off  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 212.819pt, "Laser Lift-Off (LLO) is a pivotal technique for damage-free separation of freestanding thin films. ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 232.926pt, "Its fundamental principle relies on selective energy deposition by short-pulsed lasers at an ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 253.022pt, "absorption layer within the film-transparent substrate interface: The laser penetrates the transparent ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 273.118pt, "substrate and is efficiently absorbed by the interfacial layer, triggering instantaneous thermal ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 293.283pt, "energy conversion that induces violent material vaporization and decomposition. Rapidly ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 313.379pt, "expanding gaseous products generate high-pressure impact forces (microplasma/stress waves), ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 333.545pt, "leading to complete film detachment when exceeding the interfacial binding strength (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(474.117pt, 333.545pt, "Fig. 2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(501.472pt, 333.545pt, "a, b). ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 353.641pt, "This ")
  #line-at(108.06pt, 353.641pt, "technique ")
  #line-at(170.759pt, 353.641pt, "is ")
  #line-at(195.779pt, 353.641pt, "particularly ")
  #line-at(266.878pt, 353.641pt, "suitable ")
  #line-at(320.458pt, 353.641pt, "for ")
  #line-at(351.297pt, 353.641pt, "fabricating ")
  #line-at(419.097pt, 353.641pt, "high-quality ")
  #line-at(493.49pt, 353.641pt, "single-")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 373.795pt, "crystalline/polycrystalline freestanding thin films [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(306.653pt, 373.795pt, "91-93")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(333.902pt, 373.795pt, "]. ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 401.756pt, "Since its landmark demonstration for GaN film detachment from sapphire substrates in the late ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 421.863pt, "20th century, LLO has continuously advanced optoelectronic devices [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(419.513pt, 421.863pt, "83")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(431.218pt, 421.863pt, ",")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(434.101pt, 421.863pt, "84")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(445.794pt, 421.863pt, ",")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(448.735pt, 421.863pt, "94-96")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(475.973pt, 421.863pt, "]. Its core ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 442.017pt, "mechanism involves interface-selective photothermal decomposition: The wide bandgap of ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 462.125pt, "sapphire permits ultraviolet laser transparency, while the narrow bandgap of interfacial GaN ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 482.279pt, "enables strong photon absorption. This induces transient high temperatures that decompose GaN ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 502.316pt, "into liquid gallium and nitrogen gas. Nitrogen expansion generates separation pressure, ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 522.482pt, "complemented by gallium’s interfacial lubrication effect, enabling damage-free detachment via ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 542.578pt, "post-processing. ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 570.539pt, "Early studies validated micromachining feasibility using 355-nm laser-induced thermal ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 590.705pt, "decomposition [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(148.921pt, 590.705pt, "94")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(160.556pt, 590.705pt, "]. Subsequent advances with 248-nm excimer lasers and epoxy bonding ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 610.801pt, "achieved full transfer of millimeter-scale GaN films to silicon substrates, with X-ray diffraction ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 630.955pt, "confirming preserved crystallinity [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
