  #line-at(235.559pt, 318pt, "69")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(247.194pt, 318pt, "] or integrating SiO")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.761pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(337.999pt, 318.449pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(341.873pt, 318pt, " buffers with continuous-wave lasers to ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 338.154pt, "suppress thermomechanical damage [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(248.279pt, 338.154pt, "29")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(259.973pt, 338.154pt, "] (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(271.619pt, 338.154pt, "Fig. 2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(299.756pt, 338.154pt, "a) achieves breakthroughs in Si integration and ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 358.262pt, "high-temperature CMOS compatibility, laying foundations for complex architectures. ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 386.165pt, "Laser lift-off offers several notable advantages. The selective photothermal effect within sacrificial ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 406.261pt, "layers generates delamination stress with minimal damage to the film, as exemplified by GaN ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 426.415pt, "systems, while maintaining high process selectivity. Moreover, transparent substrates such as ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 446.522pt, "sapphire can be recycled to lower fabrication costs, and the non-contact nature of the technique ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 466.676pt, "enables both large-area and patterned processing. Despite these merits, LLO still faces critical ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 486.784pt, "limitations. The process is highly sensitive, requiring precise control of laser parameters in addition ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 506.938pt, "to expensive equipment. Furthermore, residual defects often remain on the detached surfaces, ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 527.045pt, "necessitating post-treatments such as annealing. Its applicability is also restricted to configurations ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 547.199pt, "combining a transparent substrate with a strong absorber layer, where the high-pressure stress ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 567.365pt, "generated during processing may lead to cracking in ultrathin films. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 595.198pt, "2.1.2 Mechanical Exfoliation/Spalling  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 623.101pt, "Mechanical exfoliation is a widely employed method for producing freestanding thin films, and ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 643.255pt, "its principle relies on two mechanisms. The first is the direct utilization of intrinsically weak ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 663.362pt, "interlayer bonding, such as van der Waals gaps in layered materials, to achieve exfoliation through ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 683.516pt, "applied physical forces, whereas the second takes advantage of the inherently weak adhesion ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 703.624pt, "between the film and the substrate, which serves as a predefined separation plane. ")
]

