#original-page(595.276pt, 841.89pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(513.48pt, 793.74pt, "18")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 116.705pt, "mechanical exfoliation requires the work of adhesion at the interface to be significantly lower than ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 136.8pt, "the critical fracture toughness of either the film or the substrate itself, ensuring crack propagation ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 156.966pt, "along the interface rather than through the bulk of the film.  ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 184.857pt, "Furthermore, the key to achieving clean delamination lies in interface design. The fundamental ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 204.965pt, "distinction among different technical pathways resides in their approach to treating and managing ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 225.119pt, "this interface. They form a technological spectrum ranging from strategies dealing with “strong ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 245.215pt, "interfaces - forced separation” (e.g., some forms of laser lift-off and mechanical spalling) to those ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 265.38pt, "utilizing “weak interfaces - gentle separation” (e.g., remote epitaxy and atomic lift-off). The latter ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 285.476pt, "approaches pre-construct a weakly bonded interface by introducing van der Waals gaps or ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 305.642pt, "chemical modifications, drastically reducing the energy required for separation and thereby ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 325.738pt, "enabling the production of damage-free, ultrathin films, representing a leading direction in ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 345.903pt, "technological advancement.  ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 373.795pt, "Moreover, the ultimate objective of delamination is to liberate the intrinsic properties of the ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 393.902pt, "material. Once freed from substrate clamping, strain relaxation emerges as a universal and direct ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 414.056pt, "consequence. This represents not merely a geometric alteration but a functional emancipation: it ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 434.164pt, "enables polarization rotation in ferroelectric materials, modulation of magnetic anisotropy, and the ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 454.318pt, "exploration of quantum states in strongly correlated electronic systems. In summary, delamination ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 474.425pt, "technology transcends its role as a mere fabrication step, establishing itself as a potent tool for ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 494.579pt, "strain engineering and property control. ")
