  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(370.196pt, 177.062pt, "U ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(385.32pt, 177.062pt, "≈ 1.2 eV) via ARPES and ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 197.216pt, "computational verification. These approaches provide powerful tools for ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(417.354pt, 197.216pt, "in situ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(447.113pt, 197.216pt, " manipulation of ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 217.323pt, "quantum states including superconductivity and Mott insulation. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 245.215pt, "4.3 From Property Enhancement to Functional Devices ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 273.118pt, "It is particularly crucial to recognize the profound intrinsic connection between the fabrication ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 293.283pt, "pathways and the resulting functional properties. The liberation from substrates and the acquired ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 313.379pt, "freedom for strain modulation create essential conditions for restoring and optimizing the ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 333.545pt, "material’s intrinsic state. Specifically, strain relaxation releases the material from epitaxial ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 353.641pt, "constraints, allowing its lattice and electronic structures to approach their intrinsic configurations, ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 373.795pt, "thereby underpinning the enhancement of key order parameters such as ferroelectricity, magnetism, ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 393.902pt, "and superconductivity. Concurrently, the interface decoupling process effectively mitigates ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 414.056pt, "defects and pinning effects caused by strong chemical bonds. This improvement in interface ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 434.164pt, "quality helps reduce charge scattering, thereby revealing the intrinsic charge transport behavior ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 454.318pt, "and quantum phenomena of materials in the low-dimensional limit with greater clarity.  ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 482.279pt, "Furthermore, the freestanding architecture enables novel mechanical responses in traditionally ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 502.316pt, "brittle materials. Through mechanisms such as domain switching and controlled buckling, efficient ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 522.482pt, "strain energy dissipation is achieved, ultimately leading to a paradigm shift from rigidity to ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 542.578pt, "flexibility and enabling potential applications in flexible electronics. In summary, delamination ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 562.744pt, "and transfer technologies have demonstrated significant potential as powerful tools for strain ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 582.839pt, "engineering and property control. By proactively designing the two core degrees of freedom — ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 603.005pt, "“interface” and “strain” — these techniques open expansive prospects for exploring novel material ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 623.101pt, "phases and functionalities in low-dimensional systems. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 651.062pt, "5. Conclusion and Outlook ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 678.965pt, "Freestanding thin-film technology has emerged as a transformative platform that fundamentally ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 699.061pt, "reshapes materials design paradigms. As comprehensively reviewed in this work, diverse ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 719.215pt, "fabrication strategies—spanning physical delamination, chemical etching, and remote epitaxy—")
]

// arXiv source page 32
#original-page(595.276pt, 841.89pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(513.48pt, 793.74pt, "32")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 116.705pt, "enable the liberation of high-quality films from substrate constraints, while advanced transfer ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 136.8pt, "techniques facilitate precise heterointegration across arbitrary material combinations. The ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 156.966pt, "resulting substrate-free architectures unlock suppressed intrinsic properties through strain ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 177.062pt, "relaxation and interface decoupling, while simultaneously introducing unprecedented mechanical ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 197.216pt, "flexibility. These capabilities have already enabled breakthrough applications in quantum ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 217.323pt, "computing, flexible electronics, and biomedical devices. However, the most profound impact of ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 237.477pt, "this technology lies not merely in property restoration, but in the emergence of entirely new design ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 257.585pt, "freedoms that transcend conventional epitaxial limitations. This concluding section examines these ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 277.739pt, "transformative opportunities alongside critical challenges and future directions. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 305.642pt, "5.1 Geometric Control: A Post-Growth Design Paradigm ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 333.545pt, "Beyond restoring intrinsic properties through substrate liberation, freestanding thin-film ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 353.641pt, "technology uniquely enables a geometric design strategy impossible in conventional epitaxy: the ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 373.795pt, "independent control of stacking order, twist angles, and interlayer coupling. This capability ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 393.902pt, "transcends lattice-matched heteroepitaxy, where interfacial configurations are substrate-")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 414.056pt, "determined. The programmable manipulation of these geometric parameters—stacking registry, ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 434.164pt, "rotational misorientation, and interfacial strain—creates a new axis for engineering quantum ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 454.318pt, "materials. Unlike the continuous parameter space of chemical doping or applied fields, geometric ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 474.425pt, "control operates through discrete symmetry breaking and moiré potential modulation, generating ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 494.579pt, "emergent electronic structures fundamentally distinct from constituent layers. This approach ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 514.675pt, "establishes freestanding films not merely as substrate-free versions of epitaxial systems, but as an ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 534.841pt, "entirely new materials platform where structure-property relationships can be designed on demand ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 554.936pt, "through post-growth assembly rather than being predetermined during synthesis. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 582.839pt, "5.2 Remaining Challenges ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 610.801pt, "Despite these advances, the pathway toward widespread implementation faces several critical ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 630.955pt, "bottlenecks requiring systematic solutions: ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 658.799pt, "(1) Scalability and Process Control Limitations.")
  #line-at(298.612pt, 658.799pt, "While recent advances in sacrificial layers (e.g., ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 678.965pt, "Sr")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.761pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(80.404pt, 679.429pt, "4")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(84.304pt, 678.965pt, "Al")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.761pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(96.004pt, 679.429pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(99.895pt, 678.965pt, "O")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.761pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108.305pt, 679.429pt, "7")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(112.195pt, 678.965pt, ") have improved dissolution kinetics, achieving uniform, defect-free release across wafer-")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 699.061pt, "scale areas remains challenging, requiring systematic optimization of etching rates, temperature ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 719.215pt, "gradients, and interfacial stress distribution for industrial-scale production. ")
]

// arXiv source page 33
#original-page(595.276pt, 841.89pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(513.48pt, 793.74pt, "33")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 116.705pt, "(2) Transfer-Induced Contamination and Defects. Limited control over contamination, interfacial ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 136.8pt, "bubbles, and stress-induced deformation continues to compromise device performance. The ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 156.966pt, "formation of wrinkles, cracks, and residual substrate material during transfer remains a significant ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 177.062pt, "obstacle to achieving pristine interfaces required for high-performance quantum and electronic ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 197.216pt, "devices. ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 225.119pt, "(3) Technological Generality and Material Compatibility. Current techniques remain material-")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 245.215pt, "specific, with strongly bonded systems and non-oxide materials requiring breakthroughs in ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 265.38pt, "interfacial energetics and fracture mechanics control. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 293.283pt, "5.3 Future Directions and Transformative Potential ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.02pt, 321.245pt, "Realizing the full transformative potential of this technology necessitates coordinated advances ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 341.34pt, "across multiple frontiers: ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 369.243pt, "(1) Advanced Fabrication and Transfer Technologies. Future progress requires the development ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 389.339pt, "of: (i) next-generation sacrificial layers with enhanced epitaxial compatibility, reduced interfacial ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 409.505pt, "stress, and multi-functional capabilities (serving as both growth templates and rapid-release media); ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 429.601pt, "(ii) automated, damage-free transfer systems employing probe-based micro-positioning, thermally ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 449.755pt, "programmable interfaces, and vacuum-assisted integration to enable complex heterostructures ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 469.862pt, "with atomically sharp interfaces; and (iii) scalable manufacturing processes transitioning from ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 490.016pt, "laboratory demonstrations to industrial production. ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 517.919pt, "(2) Strain-Gradient and Geometric Engineering. Exploring strain-gradient-induced emergent ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 538.015pt, "phenomena and programmable geometric control (stacking configurations, twist angles, ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 558.181pt, "dimensional confinement) represents a paradigm shift from passive property preservation to active ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 578.276pt, "functionality creation. The interplay between flexoelectric/flexomagnetic effects, topological band ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 598.442pt, "restructuring, and correlated quantum states in ultra-thin geometries offers unprecedented ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 618.538pt, "opportunities for designing reconfigurable electronic and spintronic devices. ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 646.441pt, "(3) Multi-Physical Field Integration for Intelligent Systems. Integrating mechanical strain, ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 666.595pt, "electric/magnetic fields, and optical excitation will enable smart responsive systems with ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 686.702pt, "dynamically tunable properties, particularly promising for adaptive quantum sensors, ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 706.856pt, "neuromorphic computing platforms, and bio-inspired intelligent devices. ")
]

// arXiv source page 34
#original-page(595.276pt, 841.89pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(513.48pt, 793.74pt, "34")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 116.705pt, "In conclusion, freestanding thin-film technology represents a paradigm shift in the design and ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 136.8pt, "manipulation of functional thin-film materials—evolving from a strategy of substrate liberation ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 156.966pt, "toward proactive design platforms for synergistic control of structural, mechanical, and quantum ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 177.062pt, "properties. As fabrication precision, transfer fidelity, and geometric engineering converge, this ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 197.216pt, "technology stands poised to redefine the boundaries of materials manipulation, opening pathways ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 217.323pt, "to devices and functionalities that bridge atomic-scale control with macroscopic performance. The ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 237.477pt, "journey from fundamental understanding of interfacial energetics to practical implementation ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 257.585pt, "embodies the quintessential challenge and opportunity of modern materials research. ")
]

